<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 65,834 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 65,834 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 65,834 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 62,580 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			14,921	    11,380</p>
<p>    Import cargo			50,913	    51,200</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships are expected to sail and 11 to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		 Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		66,000	Johar		due</p>
<p>Gas Oil		  60,000	CSP-10	     due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    70,000	Chesapeak City   5/7</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	Capitan Miranda  6/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
